1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,571
Dinner moved. Laundry can wait. Watt If helps
rearrange three optional

2
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:09,240
chores, without turning a chatbot's guess into
an appliance command.

3
00:00:09,565 --> 00:00:13,431
This is an Alexa Plus simulation, with
fictional household data.

4
00:00:19,284 --> 00:00:21,548
Finish the dryer and dishwasher by eight,

5
00:00:21,641 --> 00:00:26,807
and charge the bike by ten. Strands runs Qwen
and calls the planning tool.

6
00:00:27,191 --> 00:00:30,383
I inspect the checked times, approve revision
one,

7
00:00:30,476 --> 00:00:32,543
and download the actual calendar.

8
00:00:32,663 --> 00:00:36,494
Now the dryer must start at nine, but quiet
hours begin at eight.

9
00:00:36,936 --> 00:00:40,825
No timetable fits. Approval and a new calendar
are blocked.

10
00:00:41,545 --> 00:00:45,643
I relax the old dryer deadline to midnight and
move quiet hours to ten.

11
00:00:45,852 --> 00:00:48,279
The nine o'clock exact start stays.

12
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:52,946
After reviewing the new times, I approve
revision three and download again.

13
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,850
These are the files that actually downloaded,

14
00:00:57,024 --> 00:01:01,715
not a fixture. Each contains three advisory
events for fictional October

15
00:01:01,784 --> 00:01:05,790
first. The corrected dryer event runs from
nine to ten.

16
00:01:06,231 --> 00:01:10,260
Stored proposal and approval hashes bind the
calendar to the reviewed

17
00:01:10,318 --> 00:01:12,977
revision. It never starts an appliance.

18
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,961
Qwen interprets the request through Strands.

19
00:01:17,344 --> 00:01:20,421
Numbered source clauses, complete instruction
checks,

20
00:01:20,479 --> 00:01:23,730
and the reused PeakShift solver constrain the
result.

21
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:28,734
Fifty-eight regression tests pass. An
independent oracle checked three

22
00:01:28,792 --> 00:01:32,739
thousand five hundred forty-six scenarios with
no mismatch.

23
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:35,502
Those checks measure these bounded workflows,

24
00:01:35,676 --> 00:01:37,766
not general language reliability.

25
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:42,135
The same application also runs with local
Ollama,

26
00:01:42,344 --> 00:01:45,293
and manual controls remain available without a
model.

27
00:01:45,804 --> 00:01:50,982
This take used the same Qwen model on a
temporary RunPod GPU through SSH.

28
00:01:51,423 --> 00:01:54,477
All loads, prices, and forecasts are invented.

29
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:58,076
There is no live Alexa connection, measured
energy saving,

30
00:01:58,111 --> 00:02:03,022
or device control. You decide; Watt If makes
the tradeoff inspectable.
